values ('c7e3a9d5-2b48-4f06-8a14-5d0e6c3b7f21', 'nutrition-research-methods', 'Nutrition Research Methods', 'This advanced undergraduate course develops the ability to ask, design, appraise, analyze, reproduce, and communicate nutrition research. Students progress from a consequential research question to a feasible protocol, integrating literature searching, causal and conceptual models, experimental and observational designs, dietary and nutrition-status measurement, qualitative and mixed methods, sampling, biostatistics, bias analysis, research ethics, open science, critical appraisal, evidence synthesis, scientific reporting, and knowledge translation. Applied laboratories use public or simulated nutrition data and culminate in a preregistered-style research proposal, reproducible analytic product, and oral defense.');

